Year = {2026},
Month = {2026 JUN 24},
Abstract = {The transformation of data-driven economic systems is key to addressing
   climate change and achieving carbon emission targets. This change has
   not only driven the production methods of enterprises, improved their
   energy efficiency, but also stimulated consumer behavior. This
   transformation will reduce the enormous challenges faced by China. Take
   ``China's Digital Village 2011-2021{''} as the sample. On this basis,
   methods such as ``fixed effects{''} modeling and mechanism analysis are
   adopted to analyze the deep mechanisms and mechanisms of the development
   accurately, a large amount of infrastructure construction and new
   technological applications require a process of adjustment and learning,
   and during this process, a significant portion of carbon dioxide
   emissions will increase in a short period. However, digital technology
   gradually permeates every step of agricultural production. Empirical
   analysis confirms that Digital Villages Construction can effectively
   curb greenhouse gas releases generated by local economic activities. In
   contrast, their greenhouse gas emissions are subject to certain
   limitations. The reason behind this is that the carbon emissions it
   generates are closely related to industrial production. The construction
   of a ``digital village{''} can optimize resource allocation and improve
   energy efficiency, but it may not fundamentally solve the high carbon
   problem in the industrialization process. In China, the more developed
   the region, the more advanced its industrial structure, and the faster
   it can popularize green and low-carbon technologies, which will help
   maximize the emission abatement potential of digital villages. In the
   meantime, by implementing strict environmental policies, relevant
   industries and enterprises can accelerate their transformation, promote
   technological and process changes, and enhance the energy-saving effect
   of ``digital villages{''}. The article believes that more funds should
   be invested in Digital Villages Construction to better promote the
   development of rural areas and ecological civilization in depth.
   Focusing on environmental protection and resource conservation, on this
   basis, a new idea of building a ``digital countryside{''} was proposed,
   and corresponding countermeasures and suggestions were put forward.},
